  "source_review_facts": [
    "Actual CString type is ATL::CStringT<wchar_t, StrTraitMFC<...>> and key input type is LPCWSTR. CPair constructs stored CString from that pointer; keys therefore retain the prefix before first NUL. Raw caller CString logical length remains separately observable.",
    "CStringElementTraits hash is unsigned 32-bit, initial zero, multiply by 33 then add each unsigned Windows wchar code unit through first NUL; equality dispatches to StringCompare.",
    "Constructor defaults are 17 bins, f32 optimal/low/high loads 0.75/0.25/2.25 and block size10. Threshold products use f32 then native size_t conversion; low thresholds below17 become zero. PickSize uses the captured ordered prime table, not inferred prime generation.",
    "Insertion, removal and rehash chain traversal/order must follow captured GetNode/NewNode/RemoveNode/FreeNode/Rehash bodies; public enumeration makes history observable.",
    "RemoveAll internally disables rehash before its IsLocked test, so this capture implementation retains bin count when cleared."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No SDK excerpts copied into this JSON or repository; bounded private excerpts remain in the CI artifacts.",
